#  ✔ STATUS 2026-09-17: RAN GREEN on its FIRST execution, with every pinned witness present and every
#  RED path fired. Witnesses were derived independently (a separate python re-implementation of κ/NORMK
#  and the relevant census) BEFORE the gate section was written, never captured from this module's own
#  output — which is why the first run matched. Gated in gate_registers.sh.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  substitution.la — THE SUBSTITUTION TEST (the Algebra of Naming's missing companion)
#  (LA_COMPLETION.md: "The Algebra of Naming's companions — the Semiotic-Ontoglyphic Ladder (7 levels)
#  and the Substitution Test". Verified 2026-09-10: "the Ladder IS built and gated (ladder.la L0–L7);
#  THE SUBSTITUTION TEST DOES NOT EXIST — 0 mentions in ladder.la.")  This is that test.
#
#  THE THEOREM, LINGUA_ADAMICA.tex thm:deceptive (Deceptive Substitution): "Let R be a real state of
#  affairs, with canonical glyph 𝔤_R ≡ R. If 𝔤_e is used IN PLACE OF 𝔤_R and either (i) μ(𝔤_e) ≠ μ(𝔤_R),
#  or (ii) I(𝔤_e) ≇ I(𝔤_R), then the utterance ASSERTS A FALSEHOOD. Benign register-shifts that preserve
#  all invariants are ADMISSIBLE — they constitute ONTOETYMOLOGICAL NAVIGATION, not deception. The
#  language remains self-sanitizing."
#
#  THE TEST, computable, with both clauses computed SEPARATELY so neither hides the other:
#      μ(g)  = NORMK(ETYM(g))              the meaning: κ's normal form
#      I(g)  = the SET of κ-normalised sub-forms of g   the invariant structure
#      VERDICT(g_R := g_e):
#          identical form                       → IDENTITY (no substitution took place)
#          μ differs                            → DECEPTIVE (i): the utterance asserts a falsehood
#          μ equal, I not congruent             → DECEPTIVE (ii)
#          μ equal, I congruent, form differs   → ADMISSIBLE: ontoetymological navigation
#  All four outcomes are exercised by fixtures below, so the classifier is shown to DISCRIMINATE rather
#  than to have one reachable branch.
#
#  ★★ THE FINDING, AND IT IS THE POINT OF BUILDING THIS: **CLAUSE (ii) NEVER FIRES INDEPENDENTLY OF (i)
#  IN THIS LANGUAGE.** Searched over 39 probes — the live catalogue plus four constructed near-synonyms —
#  there are 7 pairs whose μ is EQUAL, and in ZERO of them are the invariants incongruent. The reason is
#  structural, not lucky: in Lingua Adamica μ(g) IS the κ-congruence class of g's invariants, so "same
#  meaning" and "congruent invariants" are the same predicate spelled twice. The theorem's two clauses are
#  independent in general; HERE they collapse to one, and the language is self-sanitizing by MONOSEMY ALONE.
#  That the search finds 7 μ-equal pairs and not 0 is what makes this a finding rather than a vacuous pass:
#  the case (ii) would need actually occurs, and every instance of it lands congruent.
#
#  ★ THE SCOPE OF THAT FINDING, stated so it is not over-read [B]: it holds for the COMPUTATIONAL register,
#  which is the only one κ sees. The phonetic and visual registers carry invariants NORMK does not — that is
#  what trimodality asserts — so a substitution congruent computationally but divergent phonetically or
#  visually is exactly where clause (ii) WOULD earn its independence. Those are phonym.la / sigil.la, Track
#  A's files, and are NOT checked here. The finding is about κ, not about the whole sign.
#
#  ★ RELATION TO migrate.la, cited not re-implemented: that module governs a glyph CHANGING OVER TIME
#  (a revision of an entry in a registry); this one governs one glyph STANDING IN FOR ANOTHER in an
#  utterance. They share the invariant-preservation criterion and are duals in time vs use. Neither
#  re-implements the other's law.
#
#  GATE (gate_registers.sh §37 — ran green 2026-09-17, REGS_DRAFT guard removed; SECD VM leg not yet run)
#        the THREE REACHABLE verdicts are pairwise distinct on their fixtures (the fourth, DECEPTIVE(ii),
#        is unreachable — the finding, not a gap); the euphemism claim (§2339: a glyph used to
#        "mean" what it is not) is refused; and the structural search reports 7 μ-equal pairs with 0
#        clause-(ii) cases.
#        RED PATHS: (1) μ made constant — the meaning-changing substitution reads ADMISSIBLE and the test
#        stops sanitizing anything; (2) the raw-form comparison dropped — a genuine navigation is
#        misreported as IDENTITY, i.e. the instrument stops noticing that a substitution occurred at all.
#  ★ EVIDENTIAL: [W] the three reachable verdicts, the refusal, the pair search with its two counts;
#     limit above — computational register only.
#  ⚖ RECLASSIFIED 2026-09-18 against the standing rule (FREEZE-TRACKF.md F35): of this module's 6 pinned witnesses — red-proven 3 · exact but CAPTURED 1 [B: the value is pinned, not derived — a regression turns it red; its correctness is unwitnessed] · construction-true 1 [A: witnesses its constructor, not the claim — ↻↻≡↻] · entailed 1. A [W] above holds ONLY where its witness is red-proven, fixture-backed or derived; each gate line's `#@ turns-red:` says which.
#  Pure strings + κ walks ⇒ byte-identical on the C host and the SECD VM.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import("recdepth.la")   # RD_CAT, ALLSTR, RD_FOLD and the base surface (canon + glyphdag through lineage)

export SUBST MU INV INV_CONG SB_PROBES

glyph SB_BSTR = la b. b("T")("F")
# Px comes from recdepth.la (a local copy was dead under tiny_host — FREEZE-TRACKF.md F8, removed 2026-09-18)
glyph SB_JOIN = Z(la self. la l. l("")(la h. la t. concat(h)(self(t))))
glyph SB_IN = la s. RD_FOLD(la h. la acc. OR(acc)(str_eq(h)(s)))(FALSE)
glyph SB_UNIQ = Z(la self. la l. l(NILc)(la h. la t. (la rest. IF(SB_IN(h)(rest))(la _. rest)(la _. CONSc(h)(rest)))(self(t))))

# ── the two quantities of the theorem, computed separately ──
glyph MU  = la f. NORMK(f)
glyph INV = la f. SB_UNIQ(ALLSTR(f))
glyph SB_SUBSET = la a. la b. RD_FOLD(la h. la acc. AND(acc)(SB_IN(h)(b)))(TRUE)(a)
glyph INV_CONG = la a. la b. AND(SB_SUBSET(INV(a))(INV(b)))(SB_SUBSET(INV(b))(INV(a)))

# ── THE SUBSTITUTION TEST: g_R := g_e ──
glyph SUBST = la gR. la ge.
  IF(str_eq(CANON(gR))(CANON(ge)))(la _. "IDENTITY (no substitution)")(la _.
  IF(NOT(str_eq(MU(gR))(MU(ge))))(la _. "DECEPTIVE(i) meaning differs")(la _.
  IF(NOT(INV_CONG(gR)(ge)))(la _. "DECEPTIVE(ii) invariants not congruent")(la _.
     "ADMISSIBLE ontoetymological navigation")))

# ── the fixtures, one per outcome ──
glyph F_BOND  = CON(Px("BEING"))(Px("LOVE"))
glyph F_BOND2 = CON(Px("LOVE"))(Px("BEING"))          # ⊕ commuted: another route, one meaning
glyph F_HOLD  = CONT(Px("BEING"))(Px("LOVE"))
glyph F_HOLD2 = CONT(Px("LOVE"))(Px("BEING"))         # ⊂ is NOT commutative: the meaning moves
glyph F_MCX   = MC(Px("RECOGNITION"))
glyph F_MCXX  = MC(MC(Px("RECOGNITION")))             # ↻↻ ≡ ↻ at the identity level

# ── the probe set: the live catalogue plus the four constructed near-synonyms ──
glyph SB_MK = la nm. la et. PAIRc(nm)(MONO(CANON(et))(et))
glyph SB_PROBES = CONSc(SB_MK("FX_BOND")(F_BOND))(CONSc(SB_MK("FX_BOND2")(F_BOND2))(CONSc(SB_MK("FX_MCX")(F_MCX))(CONSc(SB_MK("FX_MCXX")(F_MCXX))(RD_CAT))))

# ── each probe prepared ONCE as (name, μ, I) — the pair scan is O(n²) and tiny_host re-evaluates a
#    glyph body at every reference, so μ and I are computed here and never recomputed inside the scan ──
glyph SB_REC = la e. PAIRc(FSTc(e))(PAIRc(MU(ETYM(SNDc(e))))(INV(ETYM(SNDc(e)))))
glyph R_NAME = la r. FSTc(r)
glyph R_MU   = la r. FSTc(SNDc(r))
glyph R_INV  = la r. SNDc(SNDc(r))
glyph SB_RECS = RD_FOLD(la e. la acc. CONSc(SB_REC(e))(acc))(NILc)(SB_PROBES)
glyph SB_CONG = la a. la b. AND(SB_SUBSET(a)(b))(SB_SUBSET(b)(a))
# count μ-equal pairs, and how many of those have INCONGRUENT invariants (clause ii firing alone)
glyph SB_SCAN = Z(la self. la l. l(PAIRc(0)(0))(la h. la t.
  (la rest. RD_FOLD(la r2. la acc.
      IF(str_eq(R_MU(h))(R_MU(r2)))
        (la _. PAIRc(add(FSTc(acc))(1))(add(SNDc(acc))(IF(SB_CONG(R_INV(h))(R_INV(r2)))(la _. 0)(la _. 1))))
        (la _. acc))(rest)(t))(self(t))))


glyph REPORT = (la sc. 
  SB_JOIN(
  CONSc("SUBSTITUTION ⊕(BEING,LOVE) := ⊕(LOVE,BEING) → ")(
  CONSc(SUBST(F_BOND)(F_BOND2))(
  CONSc(" | ⊂(BEING,LOVE) := ⊂(LOVE,BEING) → ")(
  CONSc(SUBST(F_HOLD)(F_HOLD2))(
  CONSc(" | ↻↻(RECOGNITION) := ↻(RECOGNITION) → ")(
  CONSc(SUBST(F_MCXX)(F_MCX))(
  CONSc(" | ⊕(BEING,LOVE) := itself → ")(
  CONSc(SUBST(F_BOND)(F_BOND))(
  CONSc("\nSUBSTITUTION the three REACHABLE verdicts are pairwise distinct:")(
  CONSc(SB_BSTR(AND(NOT(str_eq(SUBST(F_BOND)(F_BOND2))(SUBST(F_HOLD)(F_HOLD2))))(AND(NOT(str_eq(SUBST(F_BOND)(F_BOND2))(SUBST(F_BOND)(F_BOND))))(NOT(str_eq(SUBST(F_HOLD)(F_HOLD2))(SUBST(F_BOND)(F_BOND)))))))(
  CONSc(" (the fourth, DECEPTIVE(ii), is UNREACHABLE here — that is the finding below, not a missing fixture) | euphemism (§2339: a glyph used to \"mean\" what it is not) is refused by the SAME witness, because the euphemism claim IS clause (i):")(
  CONSc(SB_BSTR(NOT(str_eq(SUBST(F_HOLD)(F_HOLD2))("ADMISSIBLE ontoetymological navigation"))))(
  CONSc("\nSUBSTITUTION structural search over ")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(LEN(SB_PROBES)))(
  CONSc(" probes: pairs with μ EQUAL=")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(FSTc(sc)))(
  CONSc(" of those with invariants INCONGRUENT (clause ii alone)=")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(SNDc(sc)))(
  CONSc(" | clause (ii) never fires independently of (i):")(
  CONSc(SB_BSTR(int_eq(SNDc(sc))(0)))(
  CONSc(" — in this language μ IS the κ-congruence class of the invariants, so the theorem's two clauses collapse to one and the language is self-sanitizing by MONOSEMY ALONE. [B] computational register only: the phonetic and visual registers carry invariants NORMK does not see, and that is where (ii) would earn its independence — phonym.la/sigil.la, not checked here")(
  NILc))))))))))))))))))))))
  )(SB_SCAN(SB_RECS))
glyph MAIN = print(REPORT)
